Z||000000||bilbo||05-16-2001||07:49 PM||||Whats this coppers liquid gasket stuff people are talikng about using when doing exhaust manifolds??? Is this used instead of a gasket? If so how is it applied???  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-16-2001||08:05 PM||||Man that stuff works good. I used it with the gasket-helps to hold gasket in place as well-but-doesn't wash off the hands well.  I don't know the name of it, I just ask for the "copper stuff" from my parts dept.  I do know copper is part of the name of it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||NASAReeves||05-16-2001||10:58 PM||||For sure...good stuff.  I've read that it is all Ed Parks uses.  If its good enough for Ed...its good enough for me.<P>------------------<BR>Scott & Traci<BR>'88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||05-16-2001||11:26 PM||||My dad has been a mechanic his whole life, and he uses this stuff called "Accousti-seal" made by Walker.  It looks like tar, and sets like silicone, basically.  You put it on, squish the manifold on, tighten the bolts, and it hardens up with heat.  We use this in place of manifold gaskets, eliminated the ability for anything to burn out.  This stuff works awesome, I swear by it!  I lived in Washington state when he bought it, but I'm not sure if it's available everywhere in the country.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||bilbo||05-17-2001||05:22 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cozmo||05-17-2001||07:38 AM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.permatex.com/products/gaskets.asp?f_call=get_subline&prod_name=Gasketing" TARGET=_blank>http://www.permatex.com/products/gaskets.asp?f_call=get_subline&prod_name=Gasketing</A> <BR>If you use the proper stuff when putting things together you should have no problems.  Clean up threads on bolts, holes and nuts and use antiseize compound.  Torque to spec and it's done right.<BR>C02M0||||reg||14
Z||000006||stsmithgt||05-17-2001||12:37 PM||||I had my front manifold done a couple years ago.  It's time to do it again because they didn't do it correctly.  That damn recall sheet metal in there needs to seal up better.  Does anyone put a sealant of some sort on that and the gasket to seal them up?  It too expensive to fix this problem so often.  I'm afraid somethings going to burn up if I don't get my leak fixed soon before it gets worse like my spark plug wires.  I hate having a job done more then once due to workmanship.||||reg||1
